.TH ONEDRIVE-ONDEMAND-SETUP 1 "October 2026" "onedrive-ondemand" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onedrive-ondemand-setup \- set up a OneDrive Files On-Demand profile for the current user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onedrive-ondemand-setup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes \fI~/.config/<profile>/config\fR (and \fIsync_list\fR), runs
\fBonedrive \-\-confdir=\fR... once to authorise the client, and prints the
commands for the first synchronisation and for the systemd user unit. The
first \fB\-\-resync\fR is never run automatically. The unit is enabled and
started only when confirmed or with \fB\-\-enable\-service\fR.
.PP
The mount folder must be empty or absent. An existing profile with different
settings is only overwritten with \fB\-\-force\fR. Running the command again is
safe: steps that are done are reported and skipped.
.PP
Profile \fBonedrive-ondemand\fR runs as \fBonedrive-ondemand.service\fR; any
other profile as \fBonedrive-ondemand@<profile>.service\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
Run \fBonedrive-ondemand-setup \-\-help\fR for the full list:
\fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-mount\fR, \fB\-\-sync\-list\fR, \fB\-\-business\fR,
\fB\-\-application\-id\fR, \fB\-\-azure\-tenant\-id\fR, \fB\-\-use\-intune\-sso\fR,
\fB\-\-force\fR, \fB\-\-no\-auth\fR, \fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR,
\fB\-\-enable\-service\fR, \fB\-\-no\-enable\-service\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR onedrive (1),
.BR onedrive-ondemand-unmount (1),
/usr/share/doc/onedrive-ondemand/README.ondemand.md
